00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:12.520
 The patient is fully awake, fully aware.

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:14.800
 They can hear every conversation in the room.

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:16.720
 They understand their diagnosis.

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:21.440
 They feel pain, but they are entirely paralyzed.

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:23.400
 They can't do anything.

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:28.560
 They cannot move a single muscle in their body, except in most cases, vertical eye movements

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:29.960
 and blinking.

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:33.520
 They are a prisoner trapped inside their own biological shell.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:37.680
 The guide notes that nurse has established communication with these patients using blink

00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:44.440
 systems like one blink for yes, two for no, or scanning an alphabet board with their eyes.

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:46.920
 It requires immense patience.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:52.960
 It really highlights exactly why frequent meticulous neurological assessments are vital.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:55.240
 Nurses don't just check LOC wants a shift.

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:57.880
 In an ICU, they might be checking every 15 minutes.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:03.240
