00:25:50.720 --> 00:25:51.720
 Okay.

00:25:51.720 --> 00:25:53.720
 Second, irregular respirations.

00:25:53.720 --> 00:25:58.600
 You often see changed stokes breathing, which is a terrifying pattern of rapid deep breaths

00:25:58.600 --> 00:26:02.720
 followed by long periods of apnea where they stop breathing entirely.

00:26:02.720 --> 00:26:05.920
 And the third sign is a widened pulse pressure.

00:26:05.920 --> 00:26:06.920
 Yes.

00:26:06.920 --> 00:26:11.680
 The systolic blood pressure, the top number, shoots incredibly high as the body desperately

00:26:11.680 --> 00:26:14.840
 tries to force blood into the high pressure skull.

00:26:14.840 --> 00:26:19.400
 But the diastolic pressure, the bottom number, drops or stays the same.

00:26:19.400 --> 00:26:22.440
 So you might see a blood pressure of 190 over 50.

00:26:22.440 --> 00:26:27.360
 If Cushing's Triad isn't reversed immediately, physics demands an outcome.

00:26:27.360 --> 00:26:29.720
 The pressure is building inside a rigid box.

00:26:29.720 --> 00:26:31.080
 It has to go somewhere.

00:26:31.080 --> 00:26:32.680
 And there's only one way out.

00:26:32.680 --> 00:26:33.680
 Right.

00:26:33.680 --> 00:26:37.320
 Use it from the skull as the forearm and magnum, the hole at the very bottom where the spinal

00:26:37.320 --> 00:26:38.760
 cord attaches.

00:26:38.760 --> 00:26:41.040
 That event is called herniation.

00:26:41.040 --> 00:26:46.000
 The swollen brain tissue physically pushes itself down through that small opening.

00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:50.360
 As it squeezes through, it cuts off its own blood supply and catastrophically crushes the

00:26:50.360 --> 00:26:51.520
